# California appellate justices on the November 3, 2026 ballot

California voters decide whether to retain Supreme Court and Court of Appeal justices with a yes/no vote. This guide describes each justice's record on the bench with links to the opinions. It does not grade, rank, or recommend.

**How to read this.** Each justice's page has background facts with sources, automated counts compared with the same counts for their court ("baseline"), and, for justices on San Diego County ballots, a verified list of search-and-seizure cases selected by fixed rules applied to everyone. Court of Appeal justices appear on the ballot for their whole district. See the [methodology](methodology.md) for how the data was gathered and what it cannot show.

